          "date": "2026-11-23 15:03:03.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Vitaliy Kuznetsov",
          "email": "vkuznetsov@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-24 12:10:52.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "subject": "LU-21312 idl: reserve OST_MDS_MSG opcode",
        "message": "LU-21312 idl: reserve OST_MDS_MSG opcode\n\nReserve OST_MDS_MSG (24) in enum ost_cmd for an internal message\nchannel from an MDS to external services on the OSS, including\nvendor-specific services. The request carries one buffer after\nptlrpc_body that ptlrpc does not parse. Its first __u32 is a magic\nchosen by the service owner, so that several services can share\nthe opcode and a receiver can reject a message not meant for it.\nThe rest of the buffer is defined by the service.\n\nOnly the opcode value, its name in the opcode table and the wire\nchecks are added. No handler is registered, so an OSS answers the\nopcode with -EOPNOTSUPP. This relies on \"LU-19916 target: size\nhandler tables to their opcode range\"; without it the new opcode\nindexes past the end of ofd_tgt_handlers[] and mdt_io_ops[].\nAlso add OST_FALLOCATE and OST_SEEK, missing from rpc_opcode.py.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Vitaliy Kuznetsov <vkuznetsov@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I7e64d1b3e8fa383c3b2bc23beea5254155a5306f\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
